From: Eden-Doris <doris@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:47:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Eden (Doris): performance report, CPU profiler and hitch
 sampler (always on, nothing else changes)

The report, profiler and hitch sampler of Doris builds 10-29, carried over on their own so the log
shows what happens when the game drops frames, with the emulator otherwise unchanged:
- every 10 seconds in the log ("Doris perf"): frame times, CPU time per emulator thread and the
  core it ran on, CPU cluster and GPU clocks, GPU load, battery temperature; per frame draws,
  dispatches, render passes, submits, new pipelines, worker wake-ups, texture uploads (and uploads
  over GPU-drawn contents), texture cleanup removals (copied back / lost), upload volume, new staging
  buffers, GPU memory allocated and the texture cache's memory against its thresholds; and how long
  the GPU emulation thread waited for presentation frames, shaders, GPU fences, GPU memory, the cache
  locks and the game's commands; and the longest hitches with what happened in each;
- doris_profile.txt: where the GPU thread and the Vulkan worker spend their CPU time;
- doris_hitches.txt: the GPU thread's call stacks during frames over 50 ms.
Always on in this build (no settings: values saved by older Doris builds can't turn it off). The cache
lock in PrepareDraw is taken the same way (std::lock), only timed when it has to wait.

